  "comparison": [
    "All eight states show the approved wording, actions and trust values. The HUD uses the live non-Friday weekday and differs in font, weight, offsets and trust fill.",
    "i01, i02 and i08 show the live player marker, gate symbol, grid, map type and outlines. Make up Dhuhr is an existing control and changes the Masjid bar and canal-label clearance. i02 and i08 wrap navigation above the bar as pictured. The live adhan toast in i08 partly covers the make-up caption. The toast ignores pointer input, and the Dhuhr control stays visible and works.",
    "i03 to i07 show native greybox blocks, flat ground and blue sky with different camera framing from the pictured storefronts, paving, lanterns and arch. The native refusal frame shows Inn capsules and the edge of a name label. Native panels differ in opacity, type, line wrapping, spacing, button widths and border weight. i05 and i06 differ in reputation divider and label spacing. i07 uses the native page treatment for the source and learned word."
  ],
